  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile with avgpool+concat (config_009, acc=0.5176) substantially outperforms singleprofile multimodal (config_003, acc=0.4348), and in singleprofile the image-only model is very weak (0.2266) while RNA-only is moderate (0.4106). This suggests RNA is the dominant modality, but we have no multiprofile RNA-only baseline. Question: config_018 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is the direct ablation of config_009 with the image modality removed, isolating how much of the multiprofile gain is driven by RNA profile aggregation versus the image contribution. Why best next: If RNA multiprofile alone approaches ~0.50, the image modality adds little and we should focus budget on RNA encoder/aggregation variants; if it drops substantially (e.g., <0.45), the image is essential in the multiprofile regime and we should prioritize image encoder and fusion choices. This single-variable ablation maximally reduces uncertainty about the most important architectural question before committing further experiments."
}

